    "spawns": "Zone 1's creatures as data (zone-runtime step 1): the Ash Frontier's mob rows (mobs.md 7.3), moved verbatim from origins/mobs/frontier-rows.ts with the sources spelled out and the level band as numbers\n(Zone N's common creatures are level N near the town and N+1 at the edge, the named rares N+2, Dom 2026-10-08: loadZone checks every common row is [level, level+1]). Every source is public-domain folklore,\nchronicle or literature (legends-rule), no living-religion scripture. Named creatures (Hrungnir, the Mere-Mother, the bounty foes) stay on their encounters and have no row. origins/preview/mobs.golden.json pins the list.\n`openers`: a zone that is not safe opens with a fight inside 10 s of its entry (zone-rules.ts); where the data has no creature near the entry, this names the kind that stands there as a lone opener. Zone id -> row id.\nDonor: field names only (ModernUO spawn fields, Cataclysm place_monsters), nothing copied.",
    "kit": "Zone 1's kit (zone-runtime step 1): the Characters lane's zone1-kit.glb contract and how many of each node the Frontier gets. Node names are the kit's contract (public/world/kit/zone1-kit.glb); `kinds` is the\ndensity table (per: placements per 1000 m2 of zone; r: footprint; solid: collision radius per scale, 0 = walk-through; scale: min/max). The placement rule itself (deterministic per zone id, off the roads) stays in\norigins/preview/frontier-kit.ts, which reads this through loadZone.",
